Falsifies `page_tables::x86_64::the_user_va_gate_admits_only_the_aligned_low_half`.

The defect: the gate names the wrong half. This is the confinement break stated in
its shortest possible form, and it is here rather than in a subtler place because
one of the three ISA records should be the blunt one: with it, a user program may
ask the kernel to map a page at a kernel virtual address, and every downstream
check that trusts `is_user_page_virtual_address` to have already decided that question is now
deciding nothing.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(is_user_page_virtual_address::<Ia32e>(virtual_address), virtual_address & 0xfff == 0 && virtual_address
>> 47 == 0)`, on any aligned address in either half, and
`assert!(Ia32e::is_in_half(Half::Low, virtual_address) && !Ia32e::is_in_half(Half::High, virtual_address))` on any
aligned high-half address.

**The gate is shared and the proof is not.** `is_user_page_virtual_address` is one generic
function in `lib.rs`, and DECISIONS §19 has each ISA state the property itself. The
`aarch64` and `sv39` records break the same function in two other ways; the three
patches are not copies.

diff --git a/crates/page_tables/src/page_format.rs b/crates/page_tables/src/page_format.rs
--- a/crates/page_tables/src/page_format.rs
+++ b/crates/page_tables/src/page_format.rs
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
 /// assert_eq!(PAGE_SIZE, 4096);
 /// ```
 pub fn is_user_page_virtual_address<F: PageFormat>(virtual_address: u64) -> bool {
-    F::is_in_half(Half::Low, virtual_address) && virtual_address.is_multiple_of(PAGE_SIZE)
+    F::is_in_half(Half::High, virtual_address) && virtual_address.is_multiple_of(PAGE_SIZE)
 }
 
 /// **The seam between the shared walk and a hardware page-table format.**
